1. **Comprehensive and systematic evaluation scope**: The paper evaluates 9 LLMs across two core reverse engineering tasks (name recovery and type inference), multiple input representations (decompiled code and assembly code), four architectures (x86-64, x86-32, ARM, MIPS), multiple optimization levels, and both zero-shot and fine-tuned settings. This breadth of evaluation is a genuine contribution to understanding LLM capabilities in binary analysis. Similar praise appeared in the review of VulBench: "The authors have chosen a diverse range of models... This wide variety ensures a thorough comparison for LLMs" (Q3GVrWRKuB).

